# makepkg cannot source a PKGBUILD with CRLF, and it validates every vendored
# source file (gdbinit + the .patch stack) against pinned sha256sums — a Windows
# checkout (core.autocrlf) rewrites them to CRLF, changing their bytes so the
# integrity check fails. Keep the whole vendored GCC recipe LF on every platform.
Tools/gcc-toolchain/recipe/** text eol=lf
Tools/gcc-toolchain/recipe/PKGBUILD text eol=lf
